reason: the same repr rule as text/43, surfacing in a refusal sentence: the router quotes the requested name back through py_repr, Python's repr escapes the zero-width space as \u200b while the port passes the codepoint through and the projection's escape renders it as \u200b too — so the two sentences differ by one backslash. Same verdict, same wording otherwise; the difference is the repr's non-printable rule.
